Cirrus Client license (version 2)

1. What Cirrus Client is
Cirrus Client is a free launcher for Minecraft: Java Edition. It is an independent project. It is not an official Minecraft product and is not approved by or associated with Mojang Studios or Microsoft.

2. You need Minecraft
Cirrus Client does not provide, copy or unlock the game, and it does not work around buying it. You may only use it if you own Minecraft: Java Edition. Signing in with the Microsoft account that owns it proves this and is needed to play online. Playing with an offline name needs no sign-in, but it still relies on you owning the game.

3. Permission to use
You may use Cirrus Client for yourself, for free, on your own computer. You may not sell it, rent it, or share changed copies of it, and you may not remove its notices. All rights not given here stay with the project owner.

4. Your account
You sign in on Microsoft's own page. Cirrus Client never sees or stores your password. A sign-in token is kept in Windows Credential Manager on your PC so you stay signed in; signing out deletes it.

5. Offline names
Playing with an offline name is meant for singleplayer worlds and servers that run in offline mode. Do not use it to get around the rules of a server, or to play on servers that require a real account.

6. Mods and other people's content
Mods and files from Modrinth, CurseForge, Mojang and Fabric belong to their authors and come under their own licenses. Cirrus Client only downloads them for you and checks their published checksums. Install mods only from authors you trust, because a mod can do anything a program can do. You are responsible for what you install.

7. No warranty
Cirrus Client is provided as it is, without any promise that it works, is free of errors, or suits your needs. To the extent the law allows, the project owner is not liable for any loss or damage from using it, including lost worlds, crashes or account problems.

8. Third-party software
Cirrus Client includes open-source software under its own licenses. See the THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES file that comes with the project.

9. Changes
This license may change in later versions. If it does, you will be asked to accept it again.

This is a plain-language license written for the project. It is not legal advice; the project owner should have it reviewed before wide release.
